  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Members can submit bed ideas, explain their purposes, and discuss them at a short meeting.\", \"decision\": \"How should ideas for a communal bed be compared?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nMembers submit bed ideas before the meeting and group them by purpose during discussion. Shared purposes become visible across different suggestions.\nMembers agree on purposes during the meeting and then submit bed ideas that address them. Suggestions respond to criteria chosen together.\nMembers bring one bed idea and its purpose to the meeting, then combine compatible proposals. A shared plan grows from connections between concrete suggestions."
    }
  ],
